        "function": {
          "description": "Long-term memory shared across sessions (Markdown notes of one-line bullets). Actions: search {query}, read {path}, write {path, text | bullets, title?} appends one bullet (text) or up to 10 (bullets) to one note, forget {path, text} removes bullets containing text. Each bullet is one line of at most 400 characters (1000 in project/overview); put several lessons in one write as bullets. Paths: MEMORY.md (general preferences), project/<topic> (this project), tools/<tool>. Link notes with [[path]]. Write when: the user corrects you (save the rule to follow, not the mistake); the user states a preference; a decision is made (with its reason); you hit a non-obvious gotcha about the repo, environment or a tool. Never save: session summaries, task state (PR/issue numbers, statuses), facts easy to rediscover from the repo, or secrets. Asked to index or learn the codebase into memory: write one project/overview note (at most 10 bullets: purpose, architecture, how to build and test) plus the non-obvious gotchas you found, not a file or module map, and tell the user the rest is re-read from the repo each session. Writes apply to future sessions.",
